(3) The borrowing of funds from any bank or lending institution which offers the lowest available rate of interest for such loan;
(3) Contracts for goods or services entered into with a business which is the only available source of such goods or services; and
(4) Contracts entered into under circumstances which constitute an emergency situation, provided that a record explaining the emergency is prepared by the county manager and submitted to the board of ethics at its next regular meeting.
